    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Portugal has a distinguished and enduring textile and clothing manufacturing heritage that spans centuries. The country's textile industry, concentrated in regions like Guimar - es, Braga, and Porto, has built a reputation for quality craftsmanship, technical expertise, and reliable production. Portuguese factories excel at premium knitwear, shirting, denim, and sophisticated casual wear, serving both domestic brands and international fashion houses. This strong local manufacturing foundation means that Portuguese fashion brands have excellent access to high-quality production within their own country.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        However, even with Portugal's robust manufacturing sector, growing fashion brands often encounter capacity limitations. Local Portuguese factories, while excellent, may have maximum production capacities that cannot accommodate the scaling needs of successful brands expanding their collections. Additionally, Portuguese manufacturing specializes in certain product categories - premium knitwear, denim, and casual wear - while other garment types may not be produced locally at scale. This creates natural opportunities for complementary production partnerships that enable Portuguese brands to access broader manufacturing capabilities.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        SDF Clothing explicitly positions itself as a complement to Portuguese manufacturing rather than a replacement. We serve Portuguese fashion brands who have outgrown local capacity, who need specific product categories not manufactured in Portugal, or who require cost-effective production for volume collections while maintaining premium production locally for core items. This complementary approach respects Portugal's textile heritage while providing brands with the flexibility they need to grow and compete in international markets.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
        The cost advantages of Bangladesh production enable Portuguese brands to develop broader collections without compromising on quality. Brands can maintain premium Portuguese manufacturing for signature pieces while using Bangladesh production for volume basics, seasonal trends, or experimental categories. This hybrid production strategy allows Portuguese brands to optimize their cost structure while preserving the quality reputation that Portuguese manufacturing has earned globally.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Portuguese Fashion Industry Context -->
