      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Portuguese fashion brands can strategically integrate Bangladesh production into their sourcing strategy in several specific scenarios. Volume production beyond Portuguese local capacity represents the most common use case - when a brand's success creates demand that exceeds what Portuguese factories can accommodate within reasonable lead times. Rather than turning down orders or delaying delivery, brands can supplement local production with Bangladesh manufacturing to meet demand while maintaining quality standards.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Specific product categories not manufactured in Portugal present another opportunity for complementary production. While Portuguese factories excel at knitwear, denim, and casual wear, other categories like specialized activewear, technical outerwear, or certain types of accessories may not be produced locally at scale. Bangladesh manufacturing can fill these gaps, enabling Portuguese brands to offer complete collections without being limited by local manufacturing specializations.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        Cost-effective production for wider brand collections enables Portuguese brands to develop more extensive product ranges. Brands can maintain premium Portuguese manufacturing for core, signature items while using Bangladesh production for seasonal trends, volume basics, or experimental categories. This approach optimizes the cost structure while preserving the premium positioning of key collection pieces. The cost savings from Bangladesh production can be reinvested in design development, marketing, or expanding the brand's retail presence.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
        Seasonal scaling represents another strategic application of Bangladesh production. Portuguese brands experience seasonal peaks in demand - particularly for summer collections and holiday seasons. Bangladesh manufacturing provides the flexibility to scale up production during peak periods without overcommitting to local capacity year-round. This seasonal flexibility helps brands manage cash flow while ensuring they can meet demand when it matters most.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

